        "text": "fetch-tweets silence escalation: bash modulo check replaces LLM mental arithmetic",
        "level": "h2"
      }
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "The fetch-tweets skill sends a \"social silence\" escalation notification every 7 consecutive empty runs. Today at run #21, the LLM incorrectly evaluated \"21 is not a multiple of 7\" and skipped the notification. 21 ÷ 7 = 3 — it is a multiple of 7. This is the same class of error as the PR age miscalculation fixed in PR #58."
      }
    },
    "why-section": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "why-heading",
        "why-text"
      ]
    },
    "why-heading": {
      "type": "Heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "Why",
        "level": "h3"
      }
    },
    "why-text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "On 2026-10-12, consecutive_empty reached 21 (3 full weeks of silence). The escalation notification was skipped because the LLM got the modulo wrong. The operator missed the 3-week silence milestone."
      }
    },
    "what-section": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
